l +0.0008 to +0.0816. Outcome_006 has absolute mean magnitude about 0.093, so the point estimate is much larger than the 10% benchmark, but the lower bound is near zero and corresponds to only about 0.9% of the mean magnitude. Because this is a borderline, multiplicity-exposed main effect, it should not be accepted as clinically meaningful without validation; it is kept active. H54, the related feature_002=1 main-effect test of feature_052 on outcome_006, is deferred because the H9 interaction was not supported and the overall H13 signal is the more direct candidate to validate. The most informative next analyses are independent validation of H13 and completion of the feature_065 outcome_013 effect-modification tests H41, H52, and H53. All statements are dataset-specific associations and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
